# API RATE LIMITING
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Any Python script that calls external LLMs, image-generation APIs, or web
  services in a loop must route those calls through the shared RateLimiter:
  `ReluLayer/30-tools-and-ops/relulayer-engine/orchestration/rate_limiter.py`.
- Use the `ollama_local` provider policy (30-second minimum interval, 4 calls
  per minute) unless a different policy is explicitly configured.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PYTHON REGEX & SCRIPTING SAFETY MANDATES (CRITICAL)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- NEVER pass LaTeX backslash strings (e.g., `\subsection`, `\item`, `\mathcal`, `\tau`) directly as string replacements in `re.sub()`.
- ALWAYS wrap Python `re.sub()` replacement parameters in lambda callable functions: `re.sub(pattern, lambda m: r"...", text)`. This completely prevents Python `bad escape \s` PatternError crashes.
- ALWAYS use `r"""raw triple quotes"""` for multiline LaTeX blocks.
- ALWAYS maintain a `ppa6.tex.bak` backup before executing text modification passes.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# USPTO DOCUMENT FORMALITIES (37 CFR 1.84) & BUDGET
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Canvas Size: Letter (8.5 x 11 inches).
- Margins: Top >= 1.0 in, Left >= 1.0 in, Right >= 0.6 in, Bottom >= 0.4 in.
- Drawing Budget: EXACTLY 1 page per figure (11 figures = 11 drawing pages total).
- Drawing Headers: Standalone, centered bold top header (`FIG. 1`, `FIG. 2`, ..., `FIG. 11`).
- Specification Callouts: Narrative text MUST use `FIG. 1` through `FIG. 11` verbatim.
- Page Counts: Specification (`ppa6.pdf`) = 12 pages | Drawing Suite (`ppa6_drawings.pdf`) = 11 pages | Master Filing (`ppa6_master_filing.pdf`) = 23 pages.

